the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the age is *a number*.
    the risk category is *a text*.
    the is_affordable is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the approval include *a status* with *a rate*.
    the approval are listed.
    the approval for *a number* and *a text* and *a truth value* is *a second text* with *a third text* under table approval.

the table approval is, with all matches:
    age   | risk category | is_affordable | status     | rate
    >= 18 | "Medium"      | true          | "Approved" | "Best"
    >= 12 | "Medium"      | true          | "Approved" | "Standard"
    < 12  | "Low"         | true          | "Declined" | "Standard"

the knowledge base n0109_ruleorder_hitpolicy includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/0109-ruleOrder-hitpolicy.dmn".

rule approval_1 with provenance the model at decision Approval:
the approval include a status with a rate if
    the approval for the age and the risk category and the is_affordable is the status with the rate under table approval.

scenario t001 is, as stated in "0109-ruleOrder-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 001:
    the age is 19.
    the risk category is "Medium".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval expects answers ["the approval include Approved with Best", "the approval include Approved with Standard"].

scenario t002 is, as stated in "0109-ruleOrder-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 002:
    the age is 13.
    the risk category is "Medium".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval expects answers ["the approval include Approved with Standard"].

scenario t003 is, as stated in "0109-ruleOrder-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 003:
    the age is 10.
    the risk category is "Low".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_rel_approval expects answers ["the approval include Declined with Standard"].

query q_d_rel_approval is:
    the approval include which status with which rate.

